    "text": "To determine the number of friends who attended the wedding reception, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of people invited by the bride and groom.\n2. Subtract the number of invited guests from the total number of guests to find the number of friends.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total number of people invited by the bride and groom. Each of them invited 20 couples, and since a couple consists of 2 people, each of them invited:\n\\[ 20 \\text{ couples} \\times 2 \\text{ people per couple} = 40 \\text{ people} \\]\nSince there are two brides and two grooms, the total number of people invited by the bride and groom is:\n\\[ 40 \\text{ people} \\times 2 = 80 \\text{ people} \\]\n\nNext, we subtract the number of invited guests from the total number of guests to find the number of friends. The total number of guests is 180, so the number of friends is:\n\\[ 180 \\text{ people} - 80 \\text{ people} = 100 \\text{ people} \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of friends who attended the reception is:\n\\[ \\boxed{100} \\]",
